# ── Confidential client material ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The signed agreement and the platform PDF are the client's documents, not
# source code. This repository is currently PUBLIC, so they are excluded
# outright rather than trusted to a later cleanup — once a file is pushed to a
# public repo it stays in the history, and in anyone's fork, even after it is
# deleted.
#
# PLATFORM-FACTS.md is the extract of these documents that the code actually
# needs, and it is committed deliberately: it holds domain rules, not
# commercial terms.
*.docx
~$*.docx

# cfcplatform.pdf IS committed. It is the client's screen specification — the
# source of the 44-screen inventory and the numbering used in code comments
# ("Customer 12"). A team inheriting this repo needs it to know what was asked
# for. The development agreement above stays out: that one carries commercial
# terms, which the code never needs.

# ── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Turbo ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.turbo/

# ── Environment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing here yet, but the backend team will add keys. Excluded before they
# arrive rather than after.
.env
.env*.local
*.pem

# ── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Editor and OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Local agent state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Session transcripts and scratch files. Machine-specific and not useful to
# another developer.
.claude/

# ── Working notes, not product code ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This repository is PUBLIC (see the note at the top about the agreement
# documents), so what goes in is permanent and visible to anyone.
#
# `pro-admin-revisions.md` is the CLIENT'S internal revision list - their own
# wording about what they were unhappy with, and commercial decisions such as
# the Rs500 security balance. The code records what was built and why;
# the client's unedited feedback is not ours to publish.
#
# The checklists are a developer's own tracking for one round of revisions.
# ARCHITECTURE.md is what a new developer should read instead.
pro-admin-revisions.md
PRO-CHECKLIST.md
ADMIN-CHECKLIST.md
PRO-ADMIN-CHECKLIST.md
